{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CDyy7qtYeMvtfWoE4ZMrp9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Portfolio Program â€” Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1)\n2\t\n3\t> North Star (LOCKED): Build a deep, self-improving skill repository in Skill Foundry â€” model-agnostic\n4\t> cognitive skills, compositional recipes, and (later) stateful agents â€” where every skill carries a\n5\t> LOCKED North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\" sessions\n6\t> WITHOUT drifting from its designed purpose. First end-to-end proof: a recreate-a-paper recipe that\n7\t> REPRODUCES the Gelman ANOVA paper, GRADED ON ARCHITECTURE/HANDOFF SUCCESS (not reproduction fidelity).\n8\t\n9\tThis Master Plan covers ONE Foreman-ready plan set, executed as sequential per-skill WAVE-GROUPS, whose\n10\tFIRST executable wave is the Phase-0 shared infrastructure. Per-skill work here is lightweight (canary +\n11\tNorth-Star authoring), NOT a full separate researchPrime cycle (FIX-12); full per-skill cycles are for\n12\tLATER portfolio skills beyond this plan. The recreate-a-paper slice is the proof.\n13\t\n14\t> **Stage-1 Shark-Tank convergence (2026-06-20):** 3 Sharks found 3 â‰¥2-agree BLOCKERs + 2 MAJORs.\n15\t> Scope fork resolved by the user (convergence authority): **BREADTH-FIRST** â€” this plan set builds all\n16\t> five cognitive skills to production depth (full canary sets + journals), THEN the recreate-a-paper slice.\n17\t> The four non-scope findings are folded into v2 below (see \"Shark-Tank fixes applied\").\n18\t\n19\t## Shark-Tank fixes applied (v2)\n20\t- **FIX-1 (BLOCKER: Foreman gate can't host LLM-judge/numeric validators):** all three validator types\n21\t  emit **Node-TAP / pytest output with real per-test PASS events** so Foreman's `runGate` counts them\n22\t  (no vacuous-green HALT). The TAP/pytest emitter IS the shared interface (also resolves FIX-4).\n23\t- **FIX-2 (BLOCKER: done-check not deterministic):** the architecture/handoff done-check is DEFINED NOW\n24\t  (see \"NS6 deterministic done-check\" below), not deferred.\n25\t- **FIX-3 (MAJOR: substrate spike has no gate):** P0.A opens with a **Wave-0 go/no-go spike** with an\n26\t  explicit fallback if Foreman-substrate hosting of wrapped validators fails.\n27\t- **FIX-4 (MAJOR: R6 shared interface unstated):** = the TAP/pytest emitter contract above.\n28\t- **FIX-5 (MAJOR: NS4 tier table doesn't exist/untested):** the logical-tierâ†’model table is a NET-NEW\n29\t  artifact built in P0.C **with a swap test** (swap the table â†’ assert the resolved model changes; no skill\n30\t  prose edited). Replaces the scattered per-role TRIO_MODEL_<ROLE> env resolution.\n31\t- **FIX-6 (carried: canary evolution):** canary sets are **versioned alongside skill versions**; a sleep\n32\t  cycle may PROPOSE canary additions but never edit/delete existing canaries (append-only; a deletion is a\n33\t  human call) â€” so the set neither ossifies (NS1) nor is silently weakened (NS2).\n34\t- **FIX-7 (carried: A1 fallback honesty):** the deterministic-only fallback is valid ONLY for validator (iii)\n35\t  and deterministic (ii) canaries; for LLM-judged (ii) canaries an unreachable cross-family host **HALTs as\n36\t  a degraded-coverage stamp**, never silently scores same-family.\n37\t\n38\t## Shark-Tank fixes applied (v3 â€” round 2 convergence)\n39\tRound 2 (substrate-verified) found the v2 gate was sound in plumbing but unsound in semantics. v3 folds\n40\tONE governing principle + targeted fixes:\n41\t\n42\t- **PRINCIPLE-D (the deterministic-gate rule â€” resolves flaky-gate + HALT-incoherence):** the no-regression\n43\t  GATE emits TAP `ok`/`not ok` ONLY from DETERMINISTIC checks (numeric tolerance, code/unit tests, path/schema\n44\t  existence). **LLM-judge and cross-family judging are ADVISORY** â€” they write a report artifact recorded\n45\t  alongside the wave, and NEVER emit a gate verdict. Consequences: (a) a non-deterministic judge can no longer\n46\t  flip the gate GREENâ†”HALT (round-2 CLUSTER A); (b) an unreachable cross-family host can no longer HALT the\n47\t  build â€” it just records \"degraded advisory coverage\" (corrects the false v2 FIX-7; Foreman HALT is terminal,\n48\t  so judging must stay OUT of the gate path). The cross-family judge still runs when reachable; its value is a\n49\t  recorded second-origin signal, not a gate.\n50\t- **FIX-8 (anti-fabrication floor â€” resolves NS6 gameability) [v4-hardened]:** the slice done-check binds the\n51\t  end-to-end emitted statistic to the FIREWALL-VERIFIED module's output on the SAME input (tolerance-identical) â€”\n52\t  the recipe's reported number MUST equal Ramanujan's firewall'd function run on that input. PLUS a deterministic\n53\t  perturbation test (perturb input â†’ outputs change, known-sign where implied) as a secondary check. The BINDING\n54\t  (not perturbation alone) is what defeats input-proportional fabrication (e.g. output=f(input variance) with no\n55\t  ANOVA computed). FIX-8 does NOT claim to grade fidelity (honors R3); it guarantees the emitted numbers come\n56\t  from the verified analysis core, not a fabricated shortcut.\n57\t- **FIX-9 (per-skill done-floor â€” resolves Phases-1â€“5 under-specification):** EVERY cognitive skill's\n58\t  \"production depth = DONE\" is now concretely floored (see \"Per-skill done-floor\" below); Stage 2 sets the\n59\t  per-skill K/M.\n60\t- **FIX-10 (firewall-test independence â€” resolves self-authored unit tests):** Ramanujan emits the firewall's\n61\t  algorithm spec + unit tests in a context SEPARATE from (and before) the Phase-5 code that must satisfy them;\n62\t  the code build cannot edit those tests.\n63\t- **FIX-11 (prose-skill coverage path â€” resolves vacuous-green mismatch):** each validator declares (a manifest)\n64\t  which prose deliverables it graded, basename-linked so Foreman's vacuous-green guard sees real coverage; the\n65\t  P0.A Wave-0 spike MUST prove THIS prose-deliverable path passes, not just that a wrapped validator emits PASS.\n66\t- **FIX-12 [CORRECTED 2026-06-20]:** the program is NOT one monolithic Foreman plan that builds thin skills.\n67\t  Only **Phase 0 (shared infra)** is the immediate Foreman plan. **EACH cognitive skill is its OWN\n68\t  researchPrime deep-dive â†’ skill Crucible â†’ Foreman â†’ Learn cycle**, where the best-in-class METHOD is\n69\t  searched/reviewed/refined and the skill's real protocol + canaries + non-goals are forged (a structural\n70\t  done-floor alone yields a generic, mediocre skill â€” the method must come from per-skill research). This\n71\t  restores the user's original cadence (\"multiple waves of researchPrime deep-dives + crucible specific for\n72\t  each wave, with a foreman follow on\"). The program sequence lives in `PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`; the recreate-a-\n73\t  paper proof + NS1 demo are their own cycles AFTER the skills exist. (Supersedes the earlier \"lightweight,\n74\t  one plan set\" reading, which wrongly stripped per-skill method depth.)\n75\t- **FIX-13 (NS1 is gated, not asserted) [v4-hardened]:** NS1 gets its OWN homed phase (Phase 7 below), not a\n76\t  floating note. Its criterion is REGRESSION-THEN-RECOVERY, not \"non-decrease\": inject a KNOWN defect into a\n77\t  built skill (a seeded regression that fails â‰¥1 specific canary), run a real sleep cycle, and require the\n78\t  distillation to RECOVER that canary to passing â€” a no-op/rollback revision CANNOT pass (it would leave the\n79\t  injected canary failing). This gates \"measurably IMPROVES\" (NS1), distinct from \"didn't regress\" (NS2).\n80\t- **FIX-14 (journal provenance â€” resolves seeded-vs-real-use):** build-time journal entries are captured from\n81\t  GENUINE dogfood/canary EXECUTIONS of the skill (provenance-tagged per R5), NOT hand-fabricated prose. The\n82\t  done-floor term is \"genuine-execution fixture entries,\" and the FIX-13 NS1 demonstration distills ONLY from\n83\t  genuine-execution-provenance entries (so the NS1 proof is not circular and honors the North Star's\n84\t  \"its own real-use experience\" + R5 provenance-distrust).\n85\t- **FIX-15 (advisory-judge isolation â€” resolves the single-command back-door):** the advisory cross-family/LLM\n86\t  run is a SEPARATE, failure-swallowed, output-segregated process whose exit code + stdout NEVER reach the\n87\t  wave's single gate command; an unreachable advisory host is a no-op on the gate. The P0.A Wave-0 spike MUST\n88\t  explicitly prove that an UNREACHABLE advisory host leaves the deterministic gate GREEN (not just that a\n89\t  wrapped validator emits PASS).\n90\t\n91\t## Per-skill done-floor (what \"production depth / DONE\" means for EACH of Phases 1â€“5)\n92\tA cognitive skill wave-group is DONE iff ALL (TAP-gated):\n93\t1. `NORTH-STAR.md` with â‰¥3 MACHINE-CHECKABLE non-goals (each a negative canary that must FAIL the skill).\n94\t2. A frozen canary set of â‰¥K DETERMINISTIC canaries covering the skill's core capability + every non-goal\n95\t   (K set per-skill at Stage 2; cross-family/LLM-judge canaries may be added as ADVISORY, never as the gate).\n96\t3. A `journal/` of â‰¥M GENUINE-EXECUTION fixture entries (captured from real dogfood/canary runs of the\n97\t   skill, provenance-tagged per R5 â€” NOT fabricated prose) in the 7-field schema (M per-skill at Stage 2).\n98\t4. All P0 gates GREEN (handoff contract, canary eval, drift checker) + map.json registered.\n99\t\n100\t## NS6 deterministic done-check (the proof's acceptance criterion â€” LOCKED at Stage 1)\n101\tThe recreate-a-paper slice PASSES iff ALL of:\n102\t1. Every stage boundary artifact (researchâ†’planâ†’build for the slice) passes the P0.B handoff contract gate\n103\t   (schema valid Â· all artifact_refs resolve on disk Â· north_star round-trips byte-identical Â· open_questions empty).\n104\t2. The understandâ†’build firewall artifacts EXIST and are linked: a frozen algorithm spec + unit tests\n105\t   emitted by Ramanujan, and the code satisfies those unit tests (TAP PASS).\n106\t3. The recipe emits a non-empty **Assumptions Ledger** (one row per recovered/assumed tacit value).\n107\t4. The recipe RUNS end-to-end and produces the reproduction's executed numbers, AND passes the FIX-8\n108\t   DETERMINISTIC perturbation test (perturb input data â†’ outputs must change, known-sign where implied) â€”\n109\t   this forces REAL computation without grading fidelity. A numeric-tolerance grader REPORT is present as\n110\t   ADVISORY (its verdict is recorded, NOT gated â€” PRINCIPLE-D).\n111\t5. The whole done-check is itself a TAP emitter returning all-pass from DETERMINISTIC conditions 1â€“4 only\n112\t   (so Foreman gates on real checks, not on a laundered advisory verdict).\n113\t\n114\t## North-Star criteria (every plan element must serve â‰¥1; the inclusion test)\n115\t- **NS1 self-improving:** a skill measurably improves from its own journal across a sleep cycle.\n116\t- **NS2 no-regression:** a sleep revision can never ship if it regresses the skill's frozen canary set.\n117\t- **NS3 no-drift:** a sleep revision that advances a machine-checkable non-goal is rejected.\n118\t- **NS4 model-agnostic:** persona = method + LOGICAL tier; swapping the tierâ†’model table repoints the fleet.\n119\t- **NS5 clean handoffs:** every stage boundary passes the machine-checkable handoff contract.\n120\t- **NS6 the proof:** the recreate-a-paper slice reproduces Gelman ANOVA and PASSES a deterministic\n121\t  architecture/handoff done-check (NOT graded on numeric fidelity).\n122\t\n123\t## Assumption map (premortem-derived; each has a mitigation in the phases)\n124\t- A1 *gemini-cli reachable for cross-family judging* â†’ MITIGATED by capability-gated branch (deterministic-only fallback; never silent same-family). [serves NS2/NS3]\n125\t- A2 *Foreman's test-gate substrate can host arbitrary canary suites* â†’ DERISKED by Phase-0 Wave 0 spike before any skill depends on it. [serves NS2]\n126\t- A3 *