{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01C6t1uPBbJb4wEQ14HUcGKQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Portfolio Program â€” Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1): grounded summary\n\n**North Star & framing**\n- The LOCKED North Star is a deep, self-improving, model-agnostic skill repository where every skill carries its own locked North Star, journals real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\" sessions without drifting from purpose (`MASTER-PLAN.md:3-7`).\n- The first end-to-end proof is a recreate-a-paper recipe reproducing the Gelman ANOVA paper, **graded on architecture/handoff success â€” not reproduction fidelity** (`MASTER-PLAN.md:7`, `:120-121`).\n- This is ONE Foreman-ready plan set run as sequential per-skill wave-groups; the first executable wave is Phase-0 shared infrastructure (`MASTER-PLAN.md:9-12`).\n\n**Convergence decision**\n- Stage-1 Shark-Tank (2026-06-20): 3 Sharks raised 3 â‰¥2-agree BLOCKERs + 2 MAJORs; the user (convergence authority) resolved the scope fork as **BREADTH-FIRST** â€” build all five cognitive skills to production depth (full canary sets + journals) before the recreate-a-paper slice (`MASTER-PLAN.md:14-17`).\n\n**Six North-Star inclusion criteria** (every plan element must serve â‰¥1) (`MASTER-PLAN.md:114-121`)\n- NS1 self-improving Â· NS2 no-regression Â· NS3 no-drift Â· NS4 model-agnostic (persona = method + logical tier; swap the tierâ†’model table to repoint the fleet) Â· NS5 clean handoffs Â· NS6 the proof.\n\n**Governing principle from round-2 convergence**\n- PRINCIPLE-D: the no-regression GATE emits TAP `ok`/`not ok` ONLY from deterministic checks; LLM-judge and cross-family judging are **advisory** (recorded artifact, never a gate verdict). Consequence: a flaky judge can't flip the gate, and an unreachable cross-family host records \"degraded coverage\" instead of HALTing â€” because Foreman HALT is terminal (`MASTER-PLAN.md:42-49`).\n\n**Key fixes folded in (v2â€“v4)**\n- All three validator types emit real TAP/pytest PASS events so Foreman's `runGate` counts them, avoiding vacuous-green HALT (FIX-1/4) (`:20-27`).\n- The NS6 done-check is defined now, not deferred (FIX-2); the substrate spike gets a Wave-0 go/no-go gate with fallback (FIX-3) (`:23-26`).\n- A net-new logical-tierâ†’model config table with a swap test replaces scattered per-role env resolution (FIX-5) (`:28-30`).\n- Canary sets are versioned alongside skills and append-only â€” sleep may PROPOSE additions but never edit/delete (deletion is a human call) (FIX-6) (`:31-33`).\n- Anti-fabrication floor: the slice's emitted statistic is bound (tolerance-identical) to Ramanujan's firewall-verified module on the same input, plus a perturbation test â€” defeating input-proportional fabrication without grading fidelity (FIX-8) (`:50-56`).\n- **FIX-12 [CORRECTED]:** the program is NOT one monolithic plan building thin skills â€” only Phase 0 is the immediate Foreman plan; EACH cognitive skill is its own researchPrime â†’ skill-Crucible â†’ Foreman â†’ Learn cycle, restoring per-skill method depth (`:66-74`).\n- NS1 is gated, not asserted: its test is **regression-then-recovery** â€” inject a known defect failing â‰¥1 canary, run a real sleep cycle, require recovery (a no-op/rollback can't pass) (FIX-13) (`:75-79`).\n- Journal entries must be genuine-execution fixtures (provenance-tagged), not fabricated prose, so the NS1 proof isn't circular (FIX-14) (`:80-84`).\n\n**Per-skill done-floor** (TAP-gated) (`:91-98`)\n- `NORTH-STAR.md` with â‰¥3 machine-checkable non-goals (each a negative canary that must fail); a frozen set of â‰¥K deterministic canaries; a journal of â‰¥M genuine-execution entries (7-field schema); all P0 gates GREEN + `map.json` registered. K/M are set per-skill at Stage 2.\n\n**NS6 deterministic done-check (LOCKED)** (`:100-112`)\n- Slice passes iff: every stage boundary passes the handoff contract; firewall spec + unit tests exist and the code satisfies them; recipe emits a non-empty Assumptions Ledger; recipe runs end-to-end and passes the deterministic perturbation test (numeric grader is advisory only); and the done-check is itself a TAP emitter passing on conditions 1â€“4 only.\n\n**Phase sequence** (`:130-193`)\n- Phase 0 â€” shared infrastructure (~6 waves): P0.A eval harness + Wave-0 spike, P0.B handoff contract, P0.C skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table, P0.D journal + sleep loop, P0.E governance + canary versioning, P0.F citation hygiene.\n- Phases 1â€“5 â€” cognitive skills in data-flow order: Gandalf (review; built first as the review engine, breaking the A4 self-review bootstrap), Ramanujan (math/algorithm), Literature review (moved early), Data analysis, Analytic+ML code co-designed with code verification.\n- Phase 6 â€” the recreate-a-paper slice (the proof). Phase 7 â€” the NS1 self-improvement demonstration (~1 wave).\n\n**Out of scope (anti-drift)** (`:195-197`)\n- GWL harness/t2rs brain, stateful productivity/personal agents, the extend-own-paper second slice, and jumper/doc-writing/legal/propose-extensions â€” all deferred to later waves.\n\nA note on grounding: every bullet above traces to `planning/portfolio-program/crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md`. The referenced companion docs (`PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`, `TRIO-AUDIT.md`) exist in the same folder but I summarized only the Master Plan you named as the member document â€” say the word if you want those folded in."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8516,"cache_read_input_tokens":30260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8516},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef2cbc30-9f4f-4c35-8abd-b483576f8c42","uuid":"94f3caee-9b33-46f0-9d6a-8a8ec51d2a00","request_id":"req_011CcKGh5ynRoFyViG5z4oBa"}
